# Machine-readable twin of "Betrieb & Migration" in v2.0.0.md (Issue #709). The release notes and
# scripts/release-rehearsal.sh walk THIS list, in this order; a change to the steps in the notes
# changes this file in the same commit.
#
# Format:  phase | expected exit | id | kind | argument
#   expected exit: one code or a comma list; audits exit 2 when they list findings, which is information, not a failure
#   phase   pre = before the deploy (read-only), migrate = prisma migrate deploy, post = after it
#   kind    sql = psql -c on the throwaway DB, script = `pnpm tsx scripts/<arg>` in the new api image,
#           migrate = `prisma migrate deploy` as the image entrypoint runs it
# Operational steps with no exit code to prove (pg_dump, the deploy window, a sample sign-in per role)
# stay in the notes only.
#
# Notes "Betrieb & Migration", before the deploy: the permission count of the seven global system-role
# templates (Information only; on v1.18.0 expected 87 / 63 / 22 / 87 / 24 / 15 / 5 for a001..a007).
# Three data migrations of this release rewrite five of them (#836, #835, #599).
pre|0|role-templates-before-835-836-599|sql|select "id", cardinality("permissions") as permissions from "AccessRole" where "tenantId" is null order by "id";
# Deploy: the eleven migrations of v2.0.0, all additive or data-only (#836 x3, #835 x3, #842, #599 x2,
# #845, #597); pg_dump first.
migrate|0|migrate-deploy|migrate|
# After the deploy (read-only assertion): the seven global templates carry exactly the permission counts
# of SYSTEM_ROLE_PERMISSIONS (Admin 94, Manager 68, Mitarbeiter 24, Inhaber 94, Salonmanager 29,
# Personalabteilung 15, Ausbilder 5). A mismatch divides by zero, psql exits 1 and the rehearsal fails.
post|0|role-templates-after-835-836-599|sql|select 1/(case when count(*)=7 then 1 else 0 end) as templates_ok from "AccessRole" where "tenantId" is null and (("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001' and cardinality("permissions")=94) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a002' and cardinality("permissions")=68) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a003' and cardinality("permissions")=24) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a004' and cardinality("permissions")=94) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a005' and cardinality("permissions")=29) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a006' and cardinality("permissions")=15) or ("id"='00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a007' and cardinality("permissions")=5));
# After the deploy (read-only assertion, #842): no user row still carries skin, density or a retired
# theme id. A remaining row divides by zero, psql exits 1.
post|0|ui-preferences-after-842|sql|select 1/(case when count(*)=0 then 1 else 0 end) as ui_preferences_ok from "User" where jsonb_typeof("uiPreferences")='object' and (jsonb_exists("uiPreferences",'skin') or jsonb_exists("uiPreferences",'density') or "uiPreferences"->>'theme' in ('nacht','schiefer','wald'));
# After the deploy (read-only, #848): FIXED_SCHEDULE contracts whose weeklyHours differ from the sum of
# the day hours. Ids and numbers only; the script exits 0 whether or not it lists rows.
post|0|audit-848-weekly-vs-day-hours|script|audit-848-weekly-vs-day-hours.ts
# After the deploy (read-only, #961): vacation entitlement rows of years before a person's hire year.
# Ids and counts only; exit 2 lists findings, which is information, not a failure.
post|0,2|audit-961-entitlements-before-hire|script|audit-961-entitlements-before-hire.ts
